  "notes": [
    "The default bounded wait taught to loop participants is now",
    "`gator loop wait --max-seconds 360` (was 45), in the protocol, `/loop-join`,",
    "the Codex participant note and the CLI's \"keep waiting\" hint. `wait`",
    "checks the loop every 2 seconds and returns as soon as the turn arrives, so",
    "the longer limit never delays a turn: it only cuts the number of reissued",
    "`wait` calls by a factor of eight. The protocol now says this, and tells",
    "runtimes to set a tool-call time limit above the interval (Claude Code's",
    "Bash tool defaults to 2 minutes). The background watcher default (600) is"
